# Once UI codegen harness

Before generating or editing Once UI UI code in this project:

1. Read `node_modules/@once-ui-system/core/AGENTS.md`: it lists the task bundles
2. Read the closest bundle, `ai/bundles/{id}.md`, with any project files you need, in one step. It is complete (rules, component props, types, gotchas and a gold example), so write from it
3. Open `ai/components/<Name>.json` only for a component the bundle does not list, all in one step. Never open `ai/spec.json`
4. Validate output: `npx once-ui-validate-ai-code path/to/file.tsx`

## Next.js apps

Import `LayoutProvider` from `@once-ui-system/core/next`, not the package root. The root export
renders `SmartLink`, `Button href`, `Media` and the rest as plain `<a>` and `<img>`, with no error.

## Do not

- Use full documentation MDX pages for codegen (too large; use the harness)
- Use `Flex direction="column"` when `Column` works; same for `Row`
- Use `fillWidth fillHeight` when `fill` works
- Use `Card` for static panels (use the surface recipe on `Column`)

